# Problem-Solving-Logic

A structured collection of Python problem-solving exercises focused on logic, fundamentals, validation, and clean implementation.

## Overview

This repository documents a personal learning journey in Python problem solving. Each challenge is designed to strengthen reasoning, requirement analysis, and implementation skills through realistic scenarios and rule-based logic.

The repository begins with beginner-friendly fundamentals and progresses toward more structured data-processing problems, making it a practical record of growth and improvement.

## Goals

- Strengthen Python basics and problem-solving logic
- Translate business rules into working code
- Handle edge cases and validation correctly
- Improve readability and maintainability over time
- Build a portfolio of practical coding exercises

